BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Williston One Acts 2026
DTSTART:20261024T190000
DTEND:20261024T220000
DTSTAMP:20261024T143931Z
UID:ca1246b7d2ccb48267574ac4214194@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Williston One Acts 2026 is an annual short-play festival h
 osted by the Vermont Repertory Theatre. The event takes place over two wee
 kends in October 2026 at the company's permanent black-box venue\, The Rep
 \, located at 179 Commerce Street in Williston\, Vermont. The festival fea
 tures a dynamic lineup of 6 plays\, 6 directors\, and 6 distinct casts spl
 it across two consecutive weekends. To see all six short productions\, aud
 iences must attend a performance from each weekend. Tickets for the festiv
 al are $20 per weekend. Festival Schedule & Lineup Weekend 1: October 15
 –17\, 2026 The Way of All Fish (by Elaine May) Mountain Language (by Har
 old Pinter) The Author's Voice (by Richard Greenberg) Weekend 2: October 2
 2–24\, 2026 For Whom the Southern Belle Tolls (by Christopher Durang) Fi
 n & Euba (by Audrey Cefaly) I\, Chorus (by Ian McWethy) 20-30\n\nSources: 
 Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Repertory Theatre Black Box\, 179 Commerce St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/the-willis
 ton-one-acts-2026-01-09-2026-15-13-17
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vermont Tech Jam 2026
DTSTART:20261024T100000
DTEND:20261024T150000
DTSTAMP:20261024T143931Z
UID:fc7d3e22741d210adebdb5fb077549@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a job\, a degree\, a collaborator or professional 
 contacts? Find them all at… Vermont Tech Jam! Exhibitors at the Jam make
  everything from microchips to motion sensors\, robotics systems to chargi
 ng stations\, AI tools to electric aircraft. And all of them want to know 
 if you can help them — or if they can help you. Vermont Tech Jam is an a
 nnual career and tech expo\, organized by Seven Days\, that showcases some
  of Vermont’s most innovative companies. Presentations include Dartmouth
  professor Hany Farid discussing digital forensics and deepfakes.\n\nSourc
 es: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Hula\, 50 Lakeside Ave
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/vermont-te
 ch-jam-2026-08-10-2026-13-27-40
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Warm Up The Library
DTSTART:20261024T170000
DTEND:20261024T200000
DTSTAMP:20261024T143931Z
UID:29d5f5abcf3268ba11a20039de529b@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Dinner and auction to benefit the Jeudevine Memorial Library o
 n Saturday\, October 24\, 5-8 PM. $30 Suggested donation. Join us for an e
 ntertaining evening on which you choose from an array of pottery bowls mad
 e by local artists to select the bowl you wish to take home. Next\, you ha
 ve your bowl filled with soup as many times as you like. There will also b
 e homemade cornbread\, desserts and local cider. During the meal\, a silen
 t auction will be held\, allowing diners to bid on local food\, crafts\, s
 ervices\, and experiences. Winners of the auction will be announced at the
  end of the evening\, though you do not have to be there to win. The raffl
 e drawing for the Drop-a-Dime event will take place at the same time! The 
 Friends of the Jeudevine Library promote library use and enjoyment by host
 ing cultural events\, continuing education and community-based fundraisers
  to underwrite library projects and initiatives.\n\nSources: Vermont Publi
 c
LOCATION:Jeudevine Memorial Library (Parker Ladd Community Room)\, 93 N.Ma
 in Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/warm-up-th
 e-library-02-10-2026-21-54-42
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Will Evans at Après Only
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTSTAMP:20261024T143931Z
UID:48967b8a452d91d35fdff346af25b0@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Will Evans creates music as an open invitation—to drop your 
 guard\, tune in\, and move through the world a little more freely. Rooted 
 in folk tradition yet unconfined by genre\, his songs blend thoughtful\, q
 uotable lyrics with sunlit grooves and global textures\, encouraging liste
 ners to reconnect with their most honest selves. Based in Rhode Island\, t
 he singer\, songwriter\, and multi-instrumentalist has built a devoted fol
 lowing by pairing sound with intention\, most notably through his Kind Fol
 k community\, which turns shows into shared experiences of kindness\, char
 ity\, and collective uplift. Known for his dynamic live performances\, Eva
 ns weaves together acoustic guitar\, handpan\, didgeridoo\, beatboxing\, a
 nd percussion to create a fluid\, organic sound that feels both grounded a
 nd expansive. His 2025 release The Wild Unknown pushes that vision further
 \, exploring the crossroads of contemporary folk\, electronica\, and rock
 \, with collaborations from artists like Tristan Prettyman\, Dirtwire\, an
 d Moontricks. From sold-out rooms across the U.S. and Europe to stages sha
 red with Crosby & Nash\, Grace Potter\, Bruce Hornsby\,Dirtwire\, Trevor H
 all\, and Railroad Earth\, Will Evans continues to build a musical space w
 here connection comes first—and everyone belongs. Artist Group Info Will
  Evans laura@aftartists.com https://www.willevans.com/ 433 Mountain Rd Sto
 we \, Vermont 05672 Submit An Event Find out what's happening in your neck
  of the woods with Vermont Public's free Events newsletter. Email Address 
