BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Blacksmithing Workshop
DTSTART:20261024T100000
DTEND:20261024T150000
DTSTAMP:20261024T143931Z
UID:b294b8009818639c8dc7af4af4e9fc@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a day of metalworking just for teens ages 13–17!
  With workshop slots available on October 24 and November 15\, students ca
 n join us in the forge and learn about the history of metalworking and get
  hands-on experience with the primary techniques for forming\, forging\, a
 nd crafting metal objects as they make samples and finished pieces. Each p
 articipant will get to forge their own piece in our blacksmith forge and c
 omplete an additional project outside of the forge if time permits. No pri
 or metal working or blacksmithing experience is necessary\, just an excite
 ment to create something new! We’re excited to share the wonder of metal
  arts with the next generation. On the day of the workshop\, participants 
 should wear closed-toe shoes\, long pants and a long-sleeve shirt made of 
 natural fibers. Those without these things will not be permitted to work i
 n the blacksmith forge. Participants should also bring their own lunch and
  water bottle. Protective gear and equipment will be provided by the Museu
 m. For accessibility questions\, please contact us at info@lcmm.org or 802
 -475-2022.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Lake Champlain Maritime Museum\, 4472 Basin Harbor Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/youth-blac
 ksmithing-workshop-28-08-2026-14-06-19
END:VEVENT
